Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:02.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if the Earth was flat?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.30,0:00:05.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You walk for days… toward the edge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.40,0:00:06.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.20,0:00:08.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Gravity pulls you toward the center.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.20,0:00:11.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Near the edge, down tilts sideways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.20,0:00:12.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Trees lean.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.20,0:00:14.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Oceans rush to the middle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.10,0:00:15.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.30,0:00:17.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Anything this big crushes itself into a ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.90,0:00:20.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}That's why every planet is round.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.10,0:00:22.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Which way would you walk?
